# Line-ending policy.
#
# Check out and commit every text file with LF on every platform. Without
# this, git on the windows-latest CI runner (core.autocrlf=true) converts
# text files to CRLF on checkout, so byte-exact golden comparisons and
# content-hashed fixtures pass on macOS/Linux and fail only on Windows
# (seen on PR #588 and the #548 golden corpus).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Go sources and module files are always LF; gofmt expects it.
*.go     text eol=lf
go.mod   text eol=lf
go.sum   text eol=lf

# Test fixtures that are compared or hashed byte-for-byte.
*.golden text eol=lf
*.sql    text eol=lf
*.json   text eol=lf

# Shell scripts must stay LF to be executable on Unix.
*.sh     text eol=lf

# Binary assets: never convert.
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.gif    binary
*.ico    binary
*.woff   binary
*.woff2  binary
*.ttf    binary
*.otf    binary
*.wasm   binary
*.pdf    binary
*.zip    binary
*.gz     binary
